cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Astrostats"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Sciotti"
    given-names: "Davide"

repository-code: "https://github.com/davidesciotti/Astrostats"
url: "https://github.com/davidesciotti/Astrostats"
license: "MIT"

abstract: >-
  This repository contains an exercise notebook used for the April 2026 PhD course in 
  Astrostatistics at the University of Rome Tor Vergata. The notebook illustrates  
  frequentist and bayesian inference methods, model selection, and fisher-matrix 
  forecasts, using the Supernova Cosmology Project (SCP) data as a case study.

keywords:
  - statistics
  - frequentist 
  - bayesian
  - fisher-matrix
  - forecasts
  - likelihood
  - model-selection
  - mcmc